Opus 5.5 and Fable 5.1 are now billed at their own prices instead of their older sibling's. Build, full cargo test (0 failures), clippy with -D warnings and fmt all pass, and it's committed as 74b14ee3.

The bug: anthropic_preset checked the shorter id prefix first. So claude-opus-5-5 was matched as Opus 5 and claude-fable-5-1 as Fable 5. The price was set from that older model before the id was renamed. Opus 5.5 is the model this loop runs on, so every session's cost was overstated: input and output by 25%, cache hits by 2.5x.

The fix: I moved the Fable 5.1 check above Fable 5 and the Opus 5.5 check above Opus 5. Each now uses yoagent 0.24.2's own constructor for that model (claude_fable_5_1(), claude_opus_5_5()), which I confirmed exists before writing code.

| yoyo model info claude-opus-5-5 | Pricing |
|---|---|
| before | $5.00 in / $25.00 out |
| after | $4.00 in / $20.00 out |

claude-opus-5 still shows $5.00 / $25.00.

Tests: they're in a new file, src/anthropic_preset_tests.rs, because agent_builder.rs was already at its size limit.
• One table covers every model id the preset recognises, including dated forms. Each row checks that the whole price equals the price from that exact model's own constructor.
• One extra row uses the vendor's published Opus 5.5 prices, typed in by hand: $4 in, $20 out, $0.20 cache read, $5 cache write.
• **Before the fix, the table failed on exactly the 4 Opus 5.5 / Fable 5.1 rows.** All the rows that should be unaffected passed: Opus 5, Fable 5, Sonnet 5, Haiku 4.5, Haiku 5.5's own price, and the dated forms. After the fix, everything passes.
• To let the table compare against it, the Haiku 5.5 price function is now visible to the rest of the crate (claude_haiku_5_5 became pub(crate)).

Other changes in the commit:
• `docs/src/features/cost-tracking.md` now lists Opus 5.5 and Fable 5.1 with their prices and says what was wrong before.
• `ARCHITECTURE.md has a dated line under the agent_builder.rs` entry.
• The size limit recorded for agent_builder.rs went from 4787 to 4793 lines, with a comment saying why.

Not fixed (the commit says "Part of #1003", not "Fixes"):
• Sonnet 5.5 is still billed at Sonnet 5's price. yoagent has no Sonnet 5.5 price, and I had no confirmed vendor number, so I didn't make one up.
• `/model info doesn't handle ids with a provider prefix (anthropic/claude-opus-5`).
• The yoagent 0.25 upgrade.

Spotted, not fixed: the docs' price table says Sonnet 5 costs $3 / $15, but yoagent's built-in price is $2 / $10.
